        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: происходить",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "происходить (proiskhodít) — \"to happen, to take place\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Это происходит каждую зиму. Éto proiskhódit kázhduyu zímu. This happens every winter."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Imperfective; the perfective is произойти (proizoytí), past произошёл (proizoshyól): что произошло? — what happened?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "происходить (proiskhodít) is built on про-, из- and ходить \"to go\", which is inherited from Proto-Slavic xoditi (EtymDB): to come out, to come about."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
